Sylow I gives a <subgroup> of order equal to the full $p$-part of $|G|$. Sylow II says every $p$-subgroup lies in a conjugate of any Sylow $p$-subgroup; act by the <subgroup> on the Sylow cosets and use a fixed orbit because the number of cosets is prime to $p$.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= b
{parent=9e}
